# VAPT Guardrails — Go

Apply when editing handlers, middleware, or upload code. **Always-on:** F4, F8, F9, F10. **Regression:** F1, F3. An applicable failure is Critical.

## F1 — Session end

Logout revokes the token and clears server session state. A denylist fails closed.

## F3 — Uploads

Validate size, content, and structure on the server. Store a generated name. Cap decompression. Require the auth middleware. Production scans for malware.

## F4 — Authorization

Every admin or mutation route is registered behind auth middleware. A public route is registered on a separate group and is local-dev only. A route in neither group is not public.

## F8 — Object access

A same-role caller cannot read or write another owner's `{id}`. The owning service checks it. Write structs reject unknown JSON fields.

## F9 — Authentication

Auth middleware runs before the handler. JWT checks `iss`, `aud`, `exp`, and `nbf`. Fail closed.

## F10 — Audit

Audit auth, denial, admin mutation, and upload outcome. Do not log the token.
